# Commit buddy: checkpoint work without being asked

Sessions in this repo have lost work and process history because nothing was committed
(for example a legend-lab analysis that lived only under a gitignored workspace folder).
Git history is the recovery mechanism for future agents, so **commit finished stages as
you go and push them.**

## Do not ask for permission to commit

The maintainer has standing approval for commit + push in this repo. Do not pause to ask
"should I commit this?" — commit at the stage boundary and mention the SHA in your summary.
This overrides any general "only commit when asked" instruction.

## When to commit

Commit at **stage boundaries**, not on every edit:

- a feature or fix pass is coherent and self-consistent
- RL / legend feedback has been applied and reconciled
- an analysis isolation or recovery change works
- `npm run lung:generate` or `npm run lung:validate-layers` just succeeded
- **before** starting a risky refactor, so there is a known-good point to return to
- many files have piled up uncommitted, or a long stretch has passed with no commit

## How to commit

Record a stage as you finish it, then commit that workstream:

```bash
npm run buddy:note -- --workstream image-layer-analysis "Reclaimed dangling live lease"
npm run buddy:commit -- --workstream image-layer-analysis \
  --subject "Isolate legend lab analyses behind reclaimable leases." \
  --body "Test 1 lost an analysis to a stuck lease, so leases now expire and the matcher reports stderr instead of dying."
```

`buddy:commit` stages only that workstream's paths, screens out secrets and denylisted
files, refuses empty commits, and pushes the current branch (adding `-u` on first push).
Run `npm run buddy:check` first when unsure what is dirty.

## One workstream per commit

Two spun-off workstreams live in this repo and must not be mixed in a single commit:

| Workstream id | Covers |
|---------------|--------|
| `image-layer-analysis` | legend lab, lung template-match pipeline, cutaway layer assets, lung analysis data |
| `projects-transition` | Projects section UI, presentation, camera/visual transition |
| `agent-tooling` | `.cursor/` rules, skills, hooks, agents, the buddy itself |
| `site` | other site content and chrome |
| `repo` | root config (`package.json`, lockfile, README, ignore files) |

If both feature workstreams are dirty, make **two commits**. `buddy:commit` will refuse to
guess and will list the dirty workstreams instead.

## Hard limits

Never force-push, never push to `main` with `--force`, never change git config, never pass
`--no-verify`, never amend a pushed or non-buddy commit, never run interactive rebase.
Never commit `.env*`, credentials, keys, or anything under `tools/lung-legend-lab/workspace/`.

## Automatic safety net

Cursor hooks run the buddy at the end of every agent turn. If you forget, it makes a
`Checkpoint …` commit once its gates pass. Agent-authored messages are far more useful than
those fallbacks, so prefer committing deliberately.

For message style, workstream boundaries, and troubleshooting, see
`.cursor/skills/commit-buddy/SKILL.md`.
